  "question": {
    "text": "The 'Spin only’ Magnetic moment for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>Ni</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>]</mo><msup><mo> </mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>×</mo><mo> </mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> BM. (given = Atomic number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mn>28</mn></math>)</p><p>Round off your answer to the nearest integer."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "28",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the presence of ligand <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>, pairing does not occur in   <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> because pairing of electrons cannot create two vacant d-orbitals. Hence, nickel ion undergoes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> hybridisation and it has two unpaired electrons.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>8</mn></msup></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0056_1e2a944fa3fc.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 60px;\"/></p><p>No. of unpaired electron <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>The spin only magnetic moment </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>8</mn></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>82</mn><mo> </mo><mi>BM</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi>BM</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>28</mn></math></p>"
  }
}